cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "eeg-qgan: capacity-matched latent generative models for multichannel seizure EEG"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Terki
    given-names: Meriem
    affiliation: "Higher School of Computer Science, 8 Mai 1945, Sidi Bel Abbes"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MeriemTerki/eeg_qgan"
abstract: >-
  A hybrid Style-qGAN and classical controls share one frozen autoencoder,
  one critic, and one parameter budget on TUH-SZ windows. Latent fidelity,
  decoded signal fidelity, and seizure detection are scored separately.
  The defaults implement the post-audit evaluation protocol.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
keywords:
  - electroencephalography
  - seizure detection
  - generative models
  - quantum machine learning
  - TUH-SZ
